{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-algebraic-gns-embedding-interpretation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:algebraic-gns-embedding-interpretation","kind":"remark","title":"The GNS image as a type II$_1$ subfactor","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-algebraic-gns-embedding"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-algebraic-gns-embedding","tags":["von-neumann-algebra","subfactor","markov-trace","gns","interpretation"],"text":"algebraic-gns-embedding-interpretation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:algebraic-gns-embedding-interpretation\"></a><p>The image <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M := \\pi_{\\mathrm{GNS}}(H_\\infty(q))''</code> forms a finite type II<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">_1</code> von Neumann algebra. This realizes the Jones–Wenzl subfactor planar algebra. The subfactor theory machinery applies directly to the QOU algebraic data.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/algebraic-gns-embedding-interpretation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"17.21.2","page":"b/rem-algebraic-gns-embedding-interpretation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
